version: 1.0

// A callback with a LITERAL default in a numeric coordinate context: the
// parser stores callback defaults via parseStringOrReference, so the codegen
// takes the string branch (resolveCallbackWithIndex -> String) and feeds a
// String into the Float position argument -> compile error in the generated
// class. The builder resolves the same shape numerically.
// (Found while writing the CG-16/CG-17 red tests: the original coordinate
// fixture broke the whole test build through this bug.)
// This file is intentionally NOT registered in MultiProgrammable — it is
// compiled by the isolated compile-error check until the fix lands.

#cbCoordDefault programmable(idx:int=0) {
  bitmap(generated(color(4, 4, #FFFFFF))): callback("xPos", $idx) = 0, 0
}
